From: Wine Fox
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, explorer, winex11, winewayland: Tray icons in the desktop's tray under X11 too.

Under X11 the icons went into the desktop's tray over XEMBED: KDE Plasma shows them through
xembedsniproxy, which copies the icon's window, black until it was drawn again (a click) and
blurry when scaled.

The StatusNotifierItem tray of winewayland moves to win32u (sni.c), for every driver: when the
session bus has a StatusNotifierWatcher, the icons are items of it under X11 too, with the
pixels of the icon (read with GetDIBits, the alpha of the mask when it has none). explorer
serves the items on a thread of its own (WINE_SYSTRAY_SNI_SERVE); without D-Bus or a watcher
it returns at once and the icons are docked as before. The new driver entry SystrayClickPos
gives where a click on the tray is in Wine's coordinates, for the cursor that programs open
their menu at: winewayland from the outputs' logical places, winex11 from the root window's
(the pointer is warped there, which Xwayland does not know out of its windows).

